<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roxana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 340–c. 310 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Roxane</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roxana was a Bactrian noblewoman, daughter of Oxyartes, whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> married in 327 BCE. She bore his posthumous son, Alexander IV, in 323 BCE, and mother and son became pawns in the wars of Alexander's successors. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassander">Cassander</a> held them captive at Amphipolis and had both killed around 310 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roxana.jpg" alt="Roxana" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pietro Rotari · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_The_Greate_and_Roxane_by_Rotari_1756.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
